@misc{Łukawski_24222,
 abstract = {The composition consists of six short movements. In movements from one to five, I worked in the role of a composer as operator of agential tools, to generate a large corpus of music, conditioning outputs with curated pitch-class distributions. I recorded hours of such seeded improvisations, then generated, selected, and edited the material—curating fragments, removing noise, normalising durations and rhythm, and transferring them into a clear score. For this concert, Animate is presented in an arrangement for MIDI-controlled grand piano and the 4Pi organ—robotic instruments built by Godfried-Willem Raes at the Logos Foundation in Ghent.

The title carries layered meanings: to animate is to give life or motion, mate stands for companionship and also the sense of checkmate, suggesting strategy and finality. 

The piece was originally commissioned and premiered for strings and piano, by the Festival Chamber Music in Lundsgaard (Kerteminde, Denmark).
},
